        "required_age": 0,
        "is_free": false,
        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In the shadowy alleys beneath Hong Kong’s aging tenement buildings, the scent of curry fishballs lingers in the air. You are Yu Sang , a woman working at a local street food stall. As night falls, the streets grow eerily silent. One by one, the regulars leave—until it’s just you... and <i>her</i>—a customer from another world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>&quot;</strong>HONG KONG HAUNTING: FISHBALL GIRL&quot;<strong> </strong> is a first-person simulation game where you run a traditional Hong Kong street food stall, selling iconic snacks to survive. But something strange is happening. Unexplainable events begin to unfold—until finally, you’re forced to face <i>her</i>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Combining urban legends with gritty Hong Kong culture, you’ll explore narrow alleys, fog-shrouded markets, and a buried truth the creator never meant for you to find. Each fishball you serve may be a clue to the city's hidden horrors. Every footstep behind you... might not belong to the living.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" > Key Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Urban Hong Kong Horror:</strong> Inspired by real-life Hong Kong ghost stories, blending familiar night markets with an uncanny atmosphere.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Psychological Narrative:</strong> A non-linear story with player-driven choices. Can you uncover the truth? There are more than <strong>1X possible endings</strong>.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Immersive Interactions:</strong> Every action and line of dialogue may hold a clue—or a trap.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Realistic Hong Kong Aesthetics:</strong> Faithfully recreated 80s–90s Hong Kong street scenes with high-detail visuals.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Fishball Simulation:</strong> Experience life as a street food vendor. Cook, serve, survive.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Are you ready to serve a <i>special guest</i> from the other side?</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In the shadowy alleys beneath Hong Kong’s aging tenement buildings, the scent of curry fishballs lingers in the air. You are Yu Sang , a woman working at a local street food stall. As night falls, the streets grow eerily silent. One by one, the regulars leave—until it’s just you... and <i>her</i>—a customer from another world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>&quot;</strong>HONG KONG HAUNTING: FISHBALL GIRL&quot;<strong> </strong> is a first-person simulation game where you run a traditional Hong Kong street food stall, selling iconic snacks to survive. But something strange is happening. Unexplainable events begin to unfold—until finally, you’re forced to face <i>her</i>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Combining urban legends with gritty Hong Kong culture, you’ll explore narrow alleys, fog-shrouded markets, and a buried truth the creator never meant for you to find. Each fishball you serve may be a clue to the city's hidden horrors. Every footstep behind you... might not belong to the living.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" > Key Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Urban Hong Kong Horror:</strong> Inspired by real-life Hong Kong ghost stories, blending familiar night markets with an uncanny atmosphere.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Psychological Narrative:</strong> A non-linear story with player-driven choices. Can you uncover the truth? There are more than <strong>1X possible endings</strong>.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Immersive Interactions:</strong> Every action and line of dialogue may hold a clue—or a trap.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Realistic Hong Kong Aesthetics:</strong> Faithfully recreated 80s–90s Hong Kong street scenes with high-detail visuals.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Fishball Simulation:</strong> Experience life as a street food vendor. Cook, serve, survive.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Are you ready to serve a <i>special guest</i> from the other side?</p>",
